1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,006
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,925
THERE IS NO RELATION
TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

3
00:00:12,513 --> 00:00:13,931
[panting]

4
00:00:16,183 --> 00:00:17,267
[in Korean] Wait.

5
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:23,273
Karin, wait. Please, hear me out.

6
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:27,444
[panting] About earlier…

7
00:00:27,945 --> 00:00:29,863
I don't want you to misunderstand.

8
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:35,077
[in English] You came for this land?

9
00:00:36,078 --> 00:00:37,079
Ah…

10
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:40,290
The land? Ah, the land.

11
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:44,795
[sighs, speaks Korean] It's true.

12
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:46,964
At first, I came here
because I wanted the land.

13
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:49,758
Okay, so I… Ah, um, wait. Hold on.

14
00:00:51,385 --> 00:00:53,428
This land… Wait.

15
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:57,015
Please, hear me out.

16
00:00:57,099 --> 00:01:02,688
I meant to explain all this to you…

17
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:05,232
[device beeping]

18
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:06,900
[breathing heavily]

19
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:09,111
-[Karin gasps]
-You okay?

20
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:25,711
[in English] Please…

21
00:01:28,797 --> 00:01:30,007
I need you to leave.

22
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:32,634
Get out of my house…

23
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:35,679
and get off my land.

24
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:42,978
I thank you…

25
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:47,065
for everything.

26
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:15,636
EPISODE 6

27
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:18,847
[♪ sorrowful music playing]

28
00:02:42,204 --> 00:02:45,415
[stammers] Have either of you
seen Karin lately?

29
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:47,459
It's been a while…

30
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:51,630
Well, here's an idea.
Why don't we pay her a visit soon?

31
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:53,757
-[villager 1] Yeah…
-[villager 2] Sure…

32
00:02:56,468 --> 00:02:58,470
-Oh! [chuckles]
-[chuckles]

33
00:02:58,553 --> 00:02:59,971
Here's Karin!

34
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:03,517
-Oh, you're a sight for sore eyes.
-Hello! It's been ages, Karin.

35
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,018
Good to see you.

36
00:03:05,102 --> 00:03:07,020
Things have been busy lately, sorry.

37
00:03:07,104 --> 00:03:09,356
-[chuckles]
-Don't run yourself into the ground.

38
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:10,982
I won't.

39
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:12,067
I'll see you later.

40
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,987
[villager 1] Bye.

41
00:03:16,863 --> 00:03:17,864
[sighs]

42
00:03:29,084 --> 00:03:30,585
[♪ sad piano music playing]

43
00:03:39,803 --> 00:03:41,471
All right. [sniffs]

44
00:03:42,514 --> 00:03:44,516
Back to doing what I do best.

45
00:03:46,101 --> 00:03:47,102
[chuckles]

46
00:03:47,853 --> 00:03:48,854
[sighs]

47
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:56,111
Okay…

48
00:04:11,585 --> 00:04:13,503
[pen scribbling]

49
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:23,180
[in Korean] You're early.

50
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:25,974
How are you adjusting?

51
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,477
It's been a while
since you last worked on site.

52
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:33,023
This is what I used to do.

53
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:34,983
[scoffs]

54
00:04:35,066 --> 00:04:36,777
Ever the workaholic.

55
00:04:37,778 --> 00:04:39,237
Let's grab lunch later.

56
00:04:40,655 --> 00:04:41,698
[sighs]

57
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,742
[footsteps depart]

58
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:52,250
[sighs]

59
00:04:53,502 --> 00:04:55,670
[♪ pensive music playing]

60
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,601
[phone buzzes]

61
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:15,857
CHIEF - KARIN, PLEASE SUBMIT
THE DOCUMENTS I ASKED FOR

62
00:05:15,941 --> 00:05:16,942
BY NOON TOMORROW.

63
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:05,365
[in Korean] It's nice.

64
00:06:17,878 --> 00:06:21,047
[in English] Kunam, you seen Mari around?

65
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:25,510
I stopped by Serendipity
but it looks like they're closed.

66
00:06:25,594 --> 00:06:27,888
No. Have you given her a call?

67
00:06:27,971 --> 00:06:29,556
Oh, uh…

68
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,850
You know what, I have,
and she's not answering.

69
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:36,187
Same for you, right?
You haven't heard from her either?

70
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:39,441
-Right.
-Hmm.

71
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:41,484
Wonder if she's okay…

72
00:06:42,444 --> 00:06:43,737
This is weird.

73
00:06:45,947 --> 00:06:49,367
-Well, I should get going.
-Sure. Have a good one.

74
00:06:49,451 --> 00:06:50,619
Yep.

75
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:06,551
[in Korean] We restructured the layout.

76
00:07:06,635 --> 00:07:08,428
As for the first floor…

77
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:11,097
-Let's adjust this layout a little…
-Yes, sir.

78
00:07:11,181 --> 00:07:12,766
[coworker]
Sir, could you have a look at these too?

79
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:15,143
We're thinking either
Urban Latte or Urban Khaki…

80
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:16,978
Hmm.

81
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,314
What material will this be made out of?

82
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:23,610
I'll have them ready by tomorrow morning
and report back to you.

83
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:24,944
Good work.

84
00:07:25,028 --> 00:07:26,446
[employees] Good work.

85
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:47,509
[sighs]

86
00:07:49,511 --> 00:07:51,262
[phone buzzing]

87
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,225
[sighs]

88
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:02,607
Hey.

89
00:08:03,525 --> 00:08:05,860
I know you guys are busy.
Why'd you come all the way down here?

90
00:08:05,944 --> 00:08:09,447
Can't exactly chitchat…

91
00:08:09,531 --> 00:08:11,449
-[Yubin groans]
-…unless I come see you.

92
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:15,453
[Sanggi] Plus, I bet you've been
skipping your meals to keep working.

93
00:08:15,537 --> 00:08:18,498
Brought you food. Eat up.

94
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:21,251
I appreciate it. This looks delicious.

95
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:23,837
[phone buzzing]

96
00:08:29,008 --> 00:08:32,512
-What is it? Huh?
-Sorry, I'm getting a call.

97
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:34,305
-Go ahead and eat.
-Oh…

98
00:08:34,389 --> 00:08:35,390
I see.

99
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:38,435
He seems busy.

100
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:43,148
[sighs] It's good to see Yubin
back at work,

101
00:08:43,857 --> 00:08:48,611
but how did he end up
working for Sia's company?

102
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:51,656
They're like oil and water.

103
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:54,325
He's got his reasons.

104
00:08:54,409 --> 00:08:55,410
And?

105
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:57,704
Did you not know about this?

106
00:08:58,830 --> 00:09:01,666
Sia is already negotiating
with the landowners around it.

107
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:05,628
[sighs] Everyone's on board
with the redevelopment,

108
00:09:06,171 --> 00:09:08,548
and they're collecting investments.

109
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,842
He gets his career back,
and he sells off his land.

110
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:13,344
It's like killing two birds
with one stone.

111
00:09:14,429 --> 00:09:16,973
-What?
-Yubin set a condition.

112
00:09:17,057 --> 00:09:18,058
What is it?

113
00:09:18,892 --> 00:09:20,727
Yubin agreed to work at Bella Terra

114
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:22,687
in exchange for them
leaving that land alone.

115
00:09:24,606 --> 00:09:28,818
[sighs] Why does he care so much
about Charo Island?

116
00:09:28,902 --> 00:09:30,070
Beats me.

117
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:33,031
[grunts]

118
00:09:38,787 --> 00:09:39,788
[grunts]

119
00:09:57,388 --> 00:09:58,389
[in English] Huh?

120
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:00,517
When did that…

121
00:10:21,496 --> 00:10:26,042
[in Korean] How many times did someone
bump into this for it to look like this?

122
00:10:29,546 --> 00:10:30,755
[grunts]

123
00:10:41,015 --> 00:10:42,475
And to finish…

124
00:10:46,855 --> 00:10:47,981
Stars.

125
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:54,279
Good.

126
00:11:14,883 --> 00:11:16,718
[♪ sad piano music playing]

127
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:22,849
[can opening]

128
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:26,394
[in English] Whoo, it's been so long!

129
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:27,604
[in Korean] All right.

130
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:29,606
-Cheers.
-Cheers. [chuckles]

131
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:53,129
[sighs]

132
00:12:03,306 --> 00:12:04,891
[Karin, in English] <i>I'll trust you, Yubin.</i>

133
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,105
[sighs]

134
00:13:08,913 --> 00:13:10,581
[♪ music fades out]

135
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:38,026
-[engine stops]
-[car door opens, closes]

136
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:48,619
Hi, Mr. Kurokawa.

137
00:13:50,288 --> 00:13:51,289
Hi, Karin.

138
00:13:56,711 --> 00:13:58,212
[rings]

139
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:10,475
This place hasn't changed one bit.

140
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:12,435
Is that where you do your research?

141
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:13,728
It is.

142
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:18,608
I do some there… And then also,
I work in the greenhouse outside.

143
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:19,901
-[grunts]
-For the most part,

144
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:22,862
I'm still using the tools
my grandfather used before me.

145
00:14:24,072 --> 00:14:26,699
Good, good. So you won the Festa.

146
00:14:26,783 --> 00:14:29,619
I'm sorry I'm late, but congratulations.

147
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:32,163
You truly deserve it.

148
00:14:33,539 --> 00:14:34,916
Thank you very much.

149
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:39,337
To what do I owe the pleasure,
Mr. Kurokawa?

150
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:43,841
Well, in looking over some documents,

151
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:46,469
I noticed that today is your birthday,
isn't it?

152
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:47,929
-Oh…
-[chuckles]

153
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:51,349
And there's one more reason
to be celebrating.

154
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:54,352
I thought this would be
a great birthday present for you.

155
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:59,148
PROOF OF CERTIFICATION

156
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:03,945
You've officially been selected
for Green Nova's mentorship.

157
00:15:04,779 --> 00:15:05,822
Congratulations.

158
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,284
I was selected?

159
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:14,622
But I thought they still had to do
a field inspection.

160
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:17,667
It's not necessary.
You were the obvious pick.

161
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:22,088
Your strawberries really were
quite memorable, you know.

162
00:15:23,714 --> 00:15:26,342
Then, getting judged at the Festa was…

163
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:28,761
That's right, that was the evaluation.

164
00:15:30,555 --> 00:15:33,099
I have a copy of your score sheet with me,
right here.

165
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:41,357
Karin, you've done great work up to now
so keep it up.

166
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:46,487
This means a lot to me. Thank you.

167
00:15:47,071 --> 00:15:48,281
Oh, please.

168
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,491
This was your doing.

169
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,293
[♪ pensive music playing]

170
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:06,549
[Karin's grandfather]
A city slicker like you must see this

171
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:08,509
and think we live out in the sticks, huh?

172
00:16:08,593 --> 00:16:10,344
[chuckles] No, not at all.

173
00:16:10,428 --> 00:16:12,763
And thank you
for letting me stay here with you.

174
00:16:13,431 --> 00:16:16,726
-This place is actually just my speed.
-Oh.

175
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:18,561
Why wouldn't you take your work to a lab?

176
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:23,065
Well, the conditions are perfect here
and that's hard to find.

177
00:16:23,149 --> 00:16:25,109
Soil quality, the sunlight…

178
00:16:25,193 --> 00:16:27,570
They're pretty hard to recreate indoors.

179
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:35,036
Karin! Young lady,
this farm is not your playground.

180
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:38,039
I'm playing with
the strawberries, Grandfather.

181
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:41,417
And if you trample one of the seedlings,
what'll you do then?

182
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,502
There'll be less plants to play with.

183
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:47,048
She's got a good head on her shoulders.

184
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:51,135
Even running around the field like she is,
she's avoiding the plants.

185
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:53,721
It's like she's playing
with the strawberries.

186
00:16:54,222 --> 00:16:55,765
[both chuckling]

187
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,856
[Gyeongsu] She'll take over this place
one day, won't she?

188
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:07,777
Yes, I do think
it's the right thing to do.

189
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:08,945
-Hmm.
-Uh-huh.

190
00:17:12,615 --> 00:17:14,784
[both chuckling]

191
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:34,136
[grunts]

192
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:36,514
Thank you, mister.

193
00:17:38,099 --> 00:17:39,475
You're Karin, right?

194
00:17:44,939 --> 00:17:46,190
I'll see you again, Karin.

195
00:17:51,696 --> 00:17:52,780
I'll see you again, Karin.

196
00:17:53,364 --> 00:17:54,365
Please.

197
00:17:56,784 --> 00:17:57,994
Ah, that's right.

198
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:02,331
What do you think about
creating a brand for your strawberries?

199
00:18:03,833 --> 00:18:05,293
Creating a brand, sir?

200
00:18:06,294 --> 00:18:08,004
-Then doesn't that mean…
-Yes.

201
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,964
Nationwide distribution.

202
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:12,091
We could send your berries
throughout Japan.

203
00:18:14,135 --> 00:18:17,722
Don't you want more people
to experience your produce?

204
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:21,475
Thank you for your faith in me.

205
00:18:22,226 --> 00:18:25,855
Uh… Although,
I haven't perfected them yet.

206
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:28,733
They are good enough as far as
I'm concerned, Karin.

207
00:18:31,152 --> 00:18:33,571
Think it over and let me know.

208
00:18:34,864 --> 00:18:36,532
-I will.
-All right.

209
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:14,195
THE STRAWBERRIES WERE SET APART
FROM THE GREENHOUSE PRODUCTS

210
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:26,666
THE VISITORS FLOCKED
TO THE BOOTH

211
00:19:26,749 --> 00:19:29,543
DURING THE FESTA'S
BOOTH EXHIBITION

212
00:19:34,465 --> 00:19:37,468
WINNER INTERVIEW

213
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:42,765
[door opens]

214
00:19:43,474 --> 00:19:44,975
[Mari] Karin!

215
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:48,312
I think it's someone's birthday today!

216
00:19:48,396 --> 00:19:49,855
Mari. [chuckles]

217
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,400
[sighs]

218
00:19:52,483 --> 00:19:54,235
Huh? What's wrong?

219
00:19:55,111 --> 00:19:56,237
What happened?

220
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,282
-[Mari whining]
-Well, it makes sense now,

221
00:20:00,366 --> 00:20:02,159
why you don't seem like yourself.

222
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:04,954
He told me he's been drifting around
without a care in the world

223
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:07,248
and then when he came to Charo Island,
he saw me,

224
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:09,959
and that's what made him decide
he should stay here.

225
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:12,253
But we started dating
and now he wants to leave,

226
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:14,880
-so that must be the reason why, right?
-Would you stop it?

227
00:20:14,964 --> 00:20:17,758
-We're talking about Kunam, right?
-Mm-hmm.

228
00:20:19,176 --> 00:20:23,180
I'm worried about Karin.
She seems pretty out of sorts.

229
00:20:24,265 --> 00:20:25,766
Yeah, I'm worried too.

230
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:26,851
[Mari sighs]

231
00:20:27,435 --> 00:20:30,938
Splitting up, it's a really hard thing
to go through.

232
00:20:32,982 --> 00:20:35,860
That's not gonna
be a thing with us, right?

233
00:20:36,861 --> 00:20:38,946
You're going to stay here
in Japan, aren't you?

234
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:47,580
RESIDENCE CARD

235
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:49,665
-[line ringing]
-[footsteps pacing]

236
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:52,918
[sighs]

237
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:54,712
I called them too late.

238
00:20:55,421 --> 00:20:56,422
They're not answering.

239
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:57,798
I can't believe you.

240
00:20:57,882 --> 00:21:00,009
This is why I told you
to take care of it early.

241
00:21:00,092 --> 00:21:02,470
I guess I didn't realize
how the time had flown.

242
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:06,599
Someone will answer soon.
Don't hang up yet.

243
00:21:06,682 --> 00:21:08,559
[call connects]

244
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:11,604
-Oh. They picked up.
-Okay, here we go.

245
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:15,441
Uh, yes. Good afternoon.

246
00:21:15,524 --> 00:21:19,111
My working holiday visa
is going to expire soon

247
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:23,616
and I'm wondering what steps I need
to take next to extend my residency.

248
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:26,118
[public servant] <i>Those visas</i>
<i>aren't eligible to be extended.</i>

249
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:28,370
-Huh?
<i>-There's a given period</i>

250
00:21:28,454 --> 00:21:30,956
<i>in which you're supposed</i>
<i>to request a change of status.</i>

251
00:21:31,749 --> 00:21:33,417
<i>If you don't apply</i>
<i>for a standard work visa,</i>

252
00:21:33,501 --> 00:21:35,503
<i>you need to leave before yours expires.</i>

253
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:39,465
What? [stammers] You're saying
I would be overstaying without it?

254
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:42,384
"Overstay"?

255
00:21:42,468 --> 00:21:44,804
Does that mean I would get deported?

256
00:21:44,887 --> 00:21:46,847
They can't deport him…

257
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:49,266
[Kunam] Understood. Thank you.

258
00:21:51,727 --> 00:21:53,604
What are we going to do?

259
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:01,195
I'm sorry.

260
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:04,073
I should get going.

261
00:22:09,370 --> 00:22:12,540
That was weird. What the heck was that?

262
00:22:12,623 --> 00:22:14,166
Sorry to do this out of the blue.

263
00:22:14,250 --> 00:22:15,876
Oh, no, I understand.

264
00:22:16,836 --> 00:22:17,837
Go on.

265
00:22:20,631 --> 00:22:24,134
Hey, you! I texted you all day yesterday,
why'd you ignore me?

266
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:28,973
I think that we should take a break.

267
00:22:30,558 --> 00:22:32,142
-What?
-I need some space.

268
00:22:34,812 --> 00:22:36,063
It's for the best.

269
00:22:43,612 --> 00:22:45,489
[Mari, whining] <i>His visa is expiring soon,</i>

270
00:22:45,573 --> 00:22:48,701
and he doesn't wanna spend
any of his time with me at all.

271
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:51,704
This is why I was telling you I don't want

272
00:22:51,787 --> 00:22:54,623
-to get in a serious relationship!
-Mari, Mari, Mari.

273
00:22:54,707 --> 00:22:58,502
I think Kunam is serious about you too.
Something could've happened.

274
00:22:58,586 --> 00:23:00,754
-Mmm?
-Mmm.

275
00:23:02,131 --> 00:23:05,009
-That's what I thought in the beginning…
-Mm-hmm.

276
00:23:05,092 --> 00:23:06,886
[♪ quirky music playing]

277
00:23:09,638 --> 00:23:11,140
[♪ sensual music playing]

278
00:23:12,099 --> 00:23:14,101
[footsteps echoing]

279
00:23:33,162 --> 00:23:35,080
-[clerk 1 gasps] Oh, my gosh!
-[clerk 2] Oh!

280
00:23:35,164 --> 00:23:37,333
-[clerk 1] You look so handsome.
-[clerks clapping]

281
00:23:37,416 --> 00:23:39,209
Oh, this fits you perfectly.

282
00:23:39,293 --> 00:23:42,046
It looks great on you.
Makes you look like a model.

283
00:23:42,129 --> 00:23:43,672
-Oh, thank you, ma'am.
-[clerk 1] Uh-huh.

284
00:23:43,756 --> 00:23:45,925
[clerk 2] Are you shopping
for a matchmaking date?

285
00:23:46,008 --> 00:23:47,176
[Mari gasps]

286
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:50,095
-Oh, well, um… Something like that, yes.
-[clerks exclaim]

287
00:23:50,179 --> 00:23:51,847
[clerk 2]
I wonder what type of girl she is.

288
00:23:51,931 --> 00:23:53,182
[clerk 1] Oh, I'm jealous.

289
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:54,850
Wait… Were you following him?

290
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:57,394
No, no, it was a total coincidence.

291
00:23:57,478 --> 00:23:59,563
Mm-hmm. So then what?

292
00:23:59,647 --> 00:24:02,900
-I saw him meeting another woman.
-He was with a girl?

293
00:24:02,983 --> 00:24:04,944
-Mm-hmm.
-Huh?

294
00:24:05,027 --> 00:24:06,528
[♪ quirky music playing]

295
00:24:10,157 --> 00:24:11,158
[Kunam] Over here.

296
00:24:11,241 --> 00:24:13,953
-[chuckles] It's been forever.
-I know, right?

297
00:24:15,829 --> 00:24:18,832
Sorry for calling out of nowhere.
Thanks for coming.

298
00:24:18,916 --> 00:24:20,334
-Yeah.
-[chuckles]

299
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:22,753
So here it is…

300
00:24:24,213 --> 00:24:26,674
What? That's amazing!
You can ask me anything.

301
00:24:26,757 --> 00:24:27,758
-Really?
-Yeah.

302
00:24:27,841 --> 00:24:29,802
-Seriously, thank you.
-No, of course.

303
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:31,303
[both chuckle]

304
00:24:32,513 --> 00:24:34,139
[person] Give me a smile
and just let it feel natural.

305
00:24:34,223 --> 00:24:35,224
NOW CALLING…
KUNAM

306
00:24:35,307 --> 00:24:36,976
-I wanna see you do it.
-I can do that.

307
00:24:38,102 --> 00:24:40,896
-[laughs] Yeah, that's totally perfect.
-[phone buzzing]

308
00:24:44,942 --> 00:24:46,735
-Should we get going?
-Yeah.

309
00:24:47,987 --> 00:24:49,822
-[Kunam] Let's do it.
-Okay. Great.

310
00:24:54,284 --> 00:24:55,369
-Thanks.
-[Kunam] Mmm.

311
00:24:57,579 --> 00:24:58,580
[sighs]

312
00:24:59,331 --> 00:25:01,709
Was this all just so he could
get away from me?

313
00:25:05,212 --> 00:25:06,255
[Karin sighs]

314
00:25:06,922 --> 00:25:08,340
I guess I should go.

315
00:25:18,267 --> 00:25:19,685
No, stay as long as you want.

316
00:25:24,398 --> 00:25:25,399
Mari.

317
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:28,318
Cheer up, okay?

318
00:25:28,402 --> 00:25:29,403
Mm-hmm.

319
00:25:32,031 --> 00:25:33,741
I want you to cheer up too.

320
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:35,659
Hmm?

321
00:25:36,744 --> 00:25:37,745
Well…

322
00:25:40,539 --> 00:25:42,791
What I mean is that Yubin,
as far as I could tell,

323
00:25:42,875 --> 00:25:45,210
was really serious about you too.

324
00:25:48,047 --> 00:25:50,382
I know 'cause I heard it for myself.

325
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:52,134
[Kunam screaming]

326
00:25:52,760 --> 00:25:54,053
[in Korean] Darn it!

327
00:25:54,136 --> 00:25:56,764
Ugh, I'm sick of bugs.

328
00:25:56,847 --> 00:25:57,848
Ugh.

329
00:25:57,931 --> 00:26:00,142
This field work is seriously no joke.

330
00:26:01,018 --> 00:26:04,396
I mean, Karin is already so frail,
so why does she have to farm the hard way?

331
00:26:04,480 --> 00:26:06,482
Why can't she just use a greenhouse
and do it the easier way?

332
00:26:06,565 --> 00:26:07,649
[Yubin] What?

333
00:26:07,733 --> 00:26:09,777
The easier way?

334
00:26:10,819 --> 00:26:14,114
Fruits are meant to grow
with the rhythm of the seasons.

335
00:26:14,198 --> 00:26:16,408
They hold the flavor of the season.

336
00:26:16,492 --> 00:26:19,995
They're meant to take effort.

337
00:26:20,079 --> 00:26:21,830
Here, take a look.

338
00:26:21,914 --> 00:26:24,249
Look at this majestic nature.

339
00:26:24,333 --> 00:26:27,836
I want to know how delicious
strawberries would turn out

340
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:30,464
when they are grown in nature.

341
00:26:36,178 --> 00:26:37,429
[in English] He really said all of that?

342
00:26:37,513 --> 00:26:38,764
Mmm.

343
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:43,310
Okay, I'm gonna go.

344
00:26:43,393 --> 00:26:44,436
Hmm.

345
00:26:55,030 --> 00:26:56,156
[grunts]

346
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:01,453
-Oh, hi.
-Hello, Karin.

347
00:27:02,079 --> 00:27:03,622
I just need a signature from you, please.

348
00:27:03,705 --> 00:27:05,624
Yep, no problem. Thank you.

349
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:07,376
-Here. If you don't mind.
-Okay, great.

350
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:11,463
SENT FROM:
AKATSUKI CITY, FUKUOKA

351
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:13,298
-Here.
-All set.

352
00:27:13,382 --> 00:27:14,967
Your copy will be on the package.

353
00:27:16,969 --> 00:27:19,388
-Here you go. Have a good day.
-Yes. Thanks so much.

354
00:27:30,983 --> 00:27:32,025
[phone buzzes]

355
00:27:36,864 --> 00:27:40,951
YOUR PACKAGE HAS BEEN DELIVERED

356
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:46,582
Ah… [sighs]

357
00:28:23,201 --> 00:28:27,372
DEAR KARIN

358
00:28:30,626 --> 00:28:31,710
[♪ tender piano music playing]

359
00:28:49,269 --> 00:28:50,562
[Yubin, in Korean] <i>Dear Karin.</i>

360
00:29:00,781 --> 00:29:01,782
-[in English] A hot coffee?
-Yeah.

361
00:29:01,865 --> 00:29:03,325
Sure thing, coming right up.

362
00:29:15,963 --> 00:29:16,964
[in Korean] What's this?

363
00:29:22,678 --> 00:29:24,179
Birthday?

364
00:29:28,433 --> 00:29:30,268
<i>Happy birthday.</i>

365
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:35,440
<i>This is the first letter</i>
<i>I write to you, Karin.</i>

366
00:29:37,609 --> 00:29:39,444
<i>I could say these words in person…</i>

367
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:43,156
<i>But I'm writing them down in a letter</i>

368
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:46,118
<i>in hopes that it will</i>
<i>help convey my sincerity.</i>

369
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:51,164
<i>My Japanese isn't all that good,</i>

370
00:29:51,248 --> 00:29:53,166
<i>but I hope it comes through.</i>

371
00:29:57,504 --> 00:30:01,800
<i>There's something important</i>
<i>I have to tell you.</i>

372
00:30:03,468 --> 00:30:06,346
<i>I should have told you much sooner.</i>

373
00:30:06,430 --> 00:30:08,890
<i>I'm sorry I waited so long.</i>

374
00:30:11,226 --> 00:30:14,855
<i>We didn't run into each other by chance.</i>

375
00:30:15,731 --> 00:30:18,150
<i>In order to sell off my property</i>
<i>on that island,</i>

376
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:22,112
<i>I needed to get ahold of yours.</i>
<i>I was here…</i>

377
00:30:22,195 --> 00:30:23,739
[in English]
You ruined my farm, didn't you?

378
00:30:23,822 --> 00:30:27,492
[Yubin, in Korean]<i> …to win you over</i>
<i>so I could get the land.</i>

379
00:30:29,703 --> 00:30:32,330
<i>That's why I got close to you.</i>

380
00:30:34,041 --> 00:30:35,333
<i>But now…</i>

381
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:37,836
<i>I couldn't care less about it.</i>

382
00:30:39,379 --> 00:30:43,091
<i>Because now, this place has become</i>
<i>important to me.</i>

383
00:30:43,175 --> 00:30:45,427
[Karin, Yubin laughing]

384
00:30:47,471 --> 00:30:50,974
[Yubin] <i>And the people</i>
<i>who have accepted me.</i>

385
00:30:51,058 --> 00:30:52,100
[villagers chattering]

386
00:30:52,934 --> 00:30:54,519
[Yubin, in Korean] <i>And you too, Karin.</i>

387
00:30:56,354 --> 00:30:59,024
<i>I thought I was helping you out,</i>

388
00:31:00,358 --> 00:31:02,944
<i>but you were the one helping me.</i>

389
00:31:10,202 --> 00:31:12,996
<i>-I love the breakfasts we have together…</i>
-[Karin] Chopsticks go in the front.

390
00:31:13,080 --> 00:31:15,540
<i>-…with our chopsticks placed differently.</i>
-[both] Thanks for the meal.

391
00:31:17,125 --> 00:31:21,755
<i>I love driving around on your truck,</i>
<i>feeling the breeze on this island.</i>

392
00:31:23,590 --> 00:31:26,093
<i>And the night you leaned on my shoulder…</i>

393
00:31:28,136 --> 00:31:30,764
<i>It felt as if a star had fallen</i>
<i>right before me.</i>

394
00:31:31,765 --> 00:31:33,809
<i>Before I knew it, I was…</i>

395
00:31:35,185 --> 00:31:37,896
<i>wishing upon that star to stay with you.</i>

396
00:31:40,982 --> 00:31:44,194
<i>To spend these ordinary</i>
<i>yet extraordinary days with you…</i>

397
00:31:45,112 --> 00:31:47,989
<i>And stay by your side forever and ever.</i>

398
00:31:48,073 --> 00:31:49,616
-Love.
-Love.

399
00:31:50,826 --> 00:31:53,328
<i>If it means that</i>
<i>you'll get to shine bright…</i>

400
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:58,291
<i>I'm willing to remain</i>
<i>in the dark of the night.</i>

401
00:31:59,835 --> 00:32:01,670
<i>That's how much I pray</i>
<i>for you to be happy.</i>

402
00:32:06,550 --> 00:32:07,551
<i>Karin.</i>

403
00:32:08,844 --> 00:32:09,886
<i>I like you.</i>

404
00:32:11,096 --> 00:32:12,180
<i>I care about you deeply.</i>

405
00:32:12,931 --> 00:32:14,266
[Karin sniffles]

406
00:32:14,349 --> 00:32:17,477
<i>With love and respect, Yubin.</i>

407
00:32:21,314 --> 00:32:22,315
[sniffles]

408
00:33:25,253 --> 00:33:26,296
[cries]

409
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:33,803
[sniffles]

410
00:33:38,141 --> 00:33:40,060
[sobbing]

411
00:34:03,792 --> 00:34:04,793
[chuckles softly]

412
00:34:07,754 --> 00:34:08,755
[sobs]

413
00:34:15,303 --> 00:34:16,888
[♪ music fades out]

414
00:34:32,279 --> 00:34:33,363
Yubin!

415
00:34:33,905 --> 00:34:35,031
Yubin…

416
00:34:40,328 --> 00:34:44,416
DOWNTOWN REDEVELOPMENT PROJECT

417
00:34:46,334 --> 00:34:47,919
-[sighs]
-[door opens]

418
00:34:48,003 --> 00:34:50,338
-[director] Good work, everyone.
-Oh…

419
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:53,675
Hello, sir.

420
00:34:55,260 --> 00:34:59,431
When is the deadline for this model?

421
00:34:59,514 --> 00:35:01,725
In a month and a half.

422
00:35:01,808 --> 00:35:03,685
We don't have much time.

423
00:35:04,352 --> 00:35:06,104
Here's how we approach this.

424
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:08,106
-A complete overhaul.
-[snaps fingers]

425
00:35:08,189 --> 00:35:10,400
-Keep it premium.
-[employee gasps]

426
00:35:10,483 --> 00:35:13,236
Sounds like a tagline.

427
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:15,155
[laughing]

428
00:35:18,658 --> 00:35:19,784
Mr. Lee?

429
00:35:20,535 --> 00:35:21,953
Please begin.

430
00:35:22,037 --> 00:35:24,080
URBAN REGENERATION
THAT PRESERVES MEMORIES

431
00:35:24,164 --> 00:35:27,626
I'm the director in charge
of this project, Lee Yubin.

432
00:35:28,918 --> 00:35:32,631
I'd like to propose a completely new angle

433
00:35:32,714 --> 00:35:35,091
that's different from anything
we've done before.

434
00:35:35,175 --> 00:35:37,427
The market is the identity
of the neighborhood

435
00:35:37,510 --> 00:35:41,139
that has accumulated the memories
of the locals' lives.

436
00:35:41,723 --> 00:35:46,853
I believe preserving the said identity
is the essence of this project.

437
00:35:48,563 --> 00:35:49,648
We will selectively…

438
00:35:49,731 --> 00:35:51,566
That doesn't sound like him.

439
00:35:51,650 --> 00:35:56,154
He's known to get rid of anything
that misaligns with his aesthetic.

440
00:35:56,237 --> 00:35:57,989
[Yubin] The history and unique charm…

441
00:35:58,073 --> 00:35:59,324
[director] Mr. Lee.

442
00:35:59,991 --> 00:36:05,497
We heard about your groundbreaking talent.

443
00:36:06,873 --> 00:36:08,458
This is disappointing.

444
00:36:09,042 --> 00:36:11,795
What people seek from the redevelopment

445
00:36:11,878 --> 00:36:17,467
is a clean, new living space,
not some old market.

446
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:18,677
[Yubin] This redevelopment plan…

447
00:36:19,678 --> 00:36:23,848
is more than a simple business initiative.

448
00:36:23,932 --> 00:36:25,767
It's about the identity
of the neighborhood…

449
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:31,773
How's identity going to make us money?
Does it bring in advertisers?

450
00:36:33,191 --> 00:36:37,821
You're with Bella Terra, not Y:SPACE.

451
00:36:38,655 --> 00:36:41,157
I can't believe your company
lasted as long as it did.

452
00:36:44,077 --> 00:36:45,203
[director scoffs]

453
00:36:45,286 --> 00:36:47,163
Show the schedule.

454
00:36:49,374 --> 00:36:53,586
We're clearing out everything,
including the traditional market.

455
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:58,717
I want a report on the revised plan
by the end of the week.

456
00:37:05,640 --> 00:37:08,810
[♪ melancholic music playing]

457
00:37:40,842 --> 00:37:42,844
[♪ melancholic music continues]

458
00:38:13,082 --> 00:38:14,083
[♪ music ends]

459
00:38:20,006 --> 00:38:21,299
[sighs]

460
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:32,143
[♪ emotional music playing]

461
00:38:37,732 --> 00:38:39,692
[Karin, in English] <i>It's important</i>
<i>to have your own special spot.</i>

462
00:38:39,776 --> 00:38:43,321
Some place all to yourself
when you're feeling overwhelmed.

463
00:38:43,404 --> 00:38:44,864
Do you have somewhere like that?

464
00:38:44,948 --> 00:38:45,949
[in Korean] Yes.

465
00:38:47,659 --> 00:38:48,660
For me…

466
00:38:50,537 --> 00:38:51,663
This place.

467
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:53,581
[in English] Wow… That's nice.

468
00:38:53,665 --> 00:38:55,124
-[in Korean] Isn't it pretty?
-[in English] Cool.

469
00:38:55,834 --> 00:38:59,796
[in Korean] This is where I go
when things get really tough.

470
00:39:01,130 --> 00:39:03,174
If you ever come to Seoul,
I'll take you there.

471
00:39:04,217 --> 00:39:06,302
[in English] Hmm. Sounds good to me.

472
00:39:08,221 --> 00:39:11,933
KARIN

473
00:39:12,016 --> 00:39:14,018
[♪ music continues]

474
00:39:22,485 --> 00:39:23,653
[sighs]

475
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:32,912
[phone buzzing]

476
00:39:43,798 --> 00:39:45,174
[buzzing continues]

477
00:39:52,223 --> 00:39:53,224
[in Korean] Hello?

478
00:39:55,476 --> 00:39:56,477
[Karin, in English] Hello?

479
00:40:14,537 --> 00:40:15,663
[stammers]

480
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:19,125
[♪ romantic song playing]

481
00:40:28,009 --> 00:40:29,010
[in Korean] Karin.

482
00:40:30,720 --> 00:40:32,305
How did you…

483
00:40:36,059 --> 00:40:37,060
[in English] Yubin…

484
00:40:39,604 --> 00:40:40,605
[sighs]

485
00:40:43,650 --> 00:40:44,859
[in Korean] How have you been?

486
00:40:45,485 --> 00:40:47,445
[breathing heavily]

487
00:40:49,781 --> 00:40:51,407
Are you feeling okay?

488
00:40:52,367 --> 00:40:53,785
Did you get sick at all?

489
00:40:55,954 --> 00:40:59,958
[sighs] I should have told you sooner.

490
00:41:03,169 --> 00:41:06,422
I'm sorry, I… I'm really sorry.

491
00:41:08,257 --> 00:41:09,467
[in English] I read it.

492
00:41:13,888 --> 00:41:14,973
Your letter…

493
00:41:24,691 --> 00:41:26,359
[breathes shakily, whimpers]

494
00:42:04,689 --> 00:42:06,232
[Yubin, in Korean] <i>I wanted to see you.</i>

495
00:42:09,110 --> 00:42:10,570
[Karin, in English] <i>I missed you so much.</i>

496
00:42:59,118 --> 00:43:00,411
MERRY BERRY LOVE

497
00:43:00,495 --> 00:43:01,496
NEXT EPISODE

498
00:43:01,579 --> 00:43:03,206
[Yubin, in English] <i>In Korean, it's </i>gamja.

499
00:43:03,289 --> 00:43:04,540
[Karin] <i>I've always wanted to try it.</i>

500
00:43:05,166 --> 00:43:06,167
[in Korean] <i>With a boyfriend…</i>

501
00:43:06,876 --> 00:43:08,878
[in English] <i>I wish I could stay here</i>
